

HWADDR.CONF(5)       UNIX Programmer's Manual      HWADDR.CONF(5)



NAME
     hwaddr.conf - per-slot Ethernet address overrides

DESCRIPTION
     The file /etc/hwaddr.conf assigns a MAC address to a card
     slot.  The kernel reads it at device initialisation, after the
     interface is registered.  Each line is:

          slot   aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff

     as in

          1      00:08:DC:F6:00:05

     Fields are separated by spaces or tabs.  Blank lines, lines
     beginning with `#', and malformed lines are silently ignored,
     leaving the derived default in place.  A missing file is not
     an error.

     A slot with no entry gets a derived default of
     00:08:DC:F6:00:<slot>.  That is stable for one machine but
     IDENTICAL ACROSS MACHINES, so two FGX systems on the same
     network segment collide.  Pin a unique address here on each.

FILES
     /etc/hwaddr.conf

SEE ALSO
     ifconfig(8)



